# encoder: `display = 0` suppresses the DB8E output (issue #19).
# Spec: encoder.md `display` — "Set this to `0` to suppress any display output
# from this circuit." Same wording as the [display] circuit's own `display` jack,
# and the same behaviour: the circuit never writes, so the screen never activates.
# Also covers the out-of-range target (`display = 4` with one DB8E) being inert
# rather than a load error, mirroring display.md's targeting rule.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[db8e]

[encoder]
    encoder = E1.1
    smooth  = 0
    display = 0
    output  = O1

[encoder]
    encoder = E1.1
    smooth  = 0
    display = 4
    output  = O2
>>>
@0 expectdisplay D1 off
@1 turn E1.1 48
@1 expect O1 0.5 tol 1e-4
@1 expect O2 0.5 tol 1e-4
@1 expectdisplay D1 off
@2 expectdisplay D1 off
